# 🎮 AETHERIA — GAME MANAGER SYSTEM

> **The Game Manager System is the central management layer of Aetheria.**
>
> It does not create the world.
>
> It manages the world.

---

# 📌 1. OVERVIEW

The **Game Manager System** is the central system responsible for coordinating and managing all major game systems inside **Aetheria**.

The Game Manager acts as the connection between:

```text
CORE WORLD BUILDING
        │
        ▼
GAME MANAGER SYSTEM
        │
        ├── Game State
        ├── World State
        ├── Master
        ├── Heroes
        ├── Dungeon
        ├── Tower
        ├── Factions
        ├── Quests
        ├── Events
        ├── Resources
        └── Story
```

The Game Manager does not directly replace individual systems.

Instead, it coordinates them and ensures that changes made by one system can affect other systems correctly.

---

# 🌍 2. CORE PRINCIPLE

Aetheria is divided into two major layers.

```text
CORE WORLD BUILDING
        │
        ▼
WORLD DEFINITION
```

and:

```text
GAME MANAGER SYSTEM
        │
        ▼
WORLD CONDITION
```

### Core World Building

Defines what exists.

Examples:

```text
Race
Kingdom
City
Faction
Character Origin
Tower
Floor
World Location
Religion
Guild
Civilization
```

### Game Manager System

Defines what is happening.

Examples:

```text
Kingdom destroyed
Faction influence increased
Hero recruited
Quest completed
Floor cleared
Cult activity increased
NPC died
Resource depleted
Event triggered
World stability decreased
```

Therefore:

> **Core World Building defines Aetheria.**
>
> **Game Manager System manages the current state of Aetheria.**

---

# 🧠 3. GAME MANAGER ROLE

The Game Manager is the central coordinator of the game.

Its primary responsibilities are:

```text
Game Initialization
Game State Management
System Coordination
World Simulation
Event Processing
Progression Management
Data Persistence
Save / Load
Trigger Processing
Condition Processing
State Transition
```

The Game Manager should not contain every gameplay mechanic directly.

Instead:

```text
GAME MANAGER
     │
     ├── Controls
     │
     ├── Coordinates
     │
     ├── Validates
     │
     ├── Updates
     │
     └── Saves
```

while individual systems handle their own specialized logic.

