# 🎯 35. DESIGN PHILOSOPHY

The Game Manager System follows several principles.

### Principle 1 — Central Coordination

The Game Manager coordinates the game but does not own every gameplay mechanic.

### Principle 2 — Persistent State

Important changes should persist.

### Principle 3 — System Independence

Each gameplay system should remain modular.

### Principle 4 — Data Driven

Game behavior should rely on state, IDs, conditions, triggers, and modifiers rather than hard-coded story branches wherever possible.

### Principle 5 — World Consequences

Player actions should be capable of changing the world.

### Principle 6 — Expandability

New systems should be able to connect to the Game Manager without rebuilding the entire game architecture.

